{{ 'ness-contact.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  "Let's Stay Connected" — the copy column plus the store's contact form.

  The form is Shopify's own {% form 'contact' %}, so messages land in the
  store's notification email with nothing third-party in the path. The fields
  are the canonical trio — contact[name], contact[email], contact[body] — which
  Shopify reads as the sender, the reply-to address, and the message body, and
  which come back as form.name / form.email / form.body when a submission is
  rejected, so a failed post never loses what was typed. Those three are the
  only visitor-authored strings this section renders, and they are escaped on
  the way back out.

  Per PLAN.md, Editability policy: "Contact — editable: heading, body copy;
  locked: form fields, {% form 'contact' %} wiring." The field labels,
  placeholders, and button wording are therefore part of the design, not
  settings. The social row is the one addition: its four URLs have to be
  authorable or the icons have nowhere to point.

  The id="contact" anchor is deliberate — the FAQ section's "Contact Us" button
  jumps here, and scroll-margin-top clears the sticky header on arrival.

  any_social below concatenates the four URLs purely as a presence test: the
  whole social row stays hidden until at least one is filled in, so a fresh
  install never shows icons that go nowhere.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign form_id = 'NessContactForm-' | append: section.id
  assign any_social = section.settings.social_facebook | append: section.settings.social_instagram | append: section.settings.social_youtube | append: section.settings.social_x
-%}

<section
  id="contact"
  class="ness-contact"
  {% if section.settings.heading != blank %}aria-labelledby="ness-contact-heading"{% endif %}
>
  <div class="ness-contact__panel">
    <div class="ness-contact__grid">
      <div class="ness-contact__copy">
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="ness-contact__heading" id="ness-contact-heading">
            {{- section.settings.heading | escape -}}
          </h2>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
          <p class="ness-contact__body">{{ section.settings.body | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if any_social != blank -%}
          <div class="ness-contact__follow">
            {%- if section.settings.social_heading != blank -%}
              <h3 class="ness-contact__follow-heading">{{ section.settings.social_heading | escape }}</h3>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              role="list" is kept because list-style: none strips list semantics
              in Safari. The icons paint with currentColor so the token drives
              them rather than a hex baked into each path.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <ul class="ness-contact__socials" role="list">
              {%- if section.settings.social_facebook != blank -%}
                <li>
                  <a href="{{ section.settings.social_facebook }}" class="ness-contact__social" aria-label="Facebook" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                    <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M 24 12.03 C 24 5.389 18.624 0 12 0 C 5.376 0 0 5.389 0 12.03 C 0 17.853 4.128 22.701 9.6 23.82 L 9.6 15.639 L 7.2 15.639 L 7.2 12.03 L 9.6 12.03 L 9.6 9.023 C 9.6 6.701 11.484 4.812 13.8 4.812 L 16.8 4.812 L 16.8 8.421 L 14.4 8.421 C 13.74 8.421 13.2 8.962 13.2 9.624 L 13.2 12.03 L 16.8 12.03 L 16.8 15.639 L 13.2 15.639 L 13.2 24 C 19.26 23.398 24 18.274 24 12.03 Z"/></svg>
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if section.settings.social_instagram != blank -%}
                <li>
                  <a href="{{ section.settings.social_instagram }}" class="ness-contact__social" aria-label="Instagram" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="20" rx="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4.6"/><circle cx="17.8" cy="6.2" r="1.2" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg>
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if section.settings.social_youtube != blank -%}
                <li>
                  <a href="{{ section.settings.social_youtube }}" class="ness-contact__social" aria-label="YouTube" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21.6 7.2c-.2-1-.9-1.7-1.9-1.9C17.9 5 12 5 12 5s-5.9 0-7.7.3c-1 .2-1.7.9-1.9 1.9C2.1 9 2.1 12 2.1 12s0 3 .3 4.8c.2 1 .9 1.7 1.9 1.9C6.1 19 12 19 12 19s5.9 0 7.7-.3c1-.2 1.7-.9 1.9-1.9.3-1.8.3-4.8.3-4.8s0-3-.3-4.8ZM9.9 15.3V8.7l5.6 3.3-5.6 3.3Z"/></svg>
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if section.settings.social_x != blank -%}
                <li>
                  <a href="{{ section.settings.social_x }}" class="ness-contact__social" aria-label="X" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                    <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 13.224 13.515" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M 7.87 5.723 L 12.793 0 L 11.627 0 L 7.352 4.969 L 3.938 0 L 0 0 L 5.163 7.514 L 0 13.515 L 1.167 13.515 L 5.681 8.268 L 9.286 13.515 L 13.224 13.515 L 7.87 5.723 L 7.87 5.723 Z M 1.587 0.878 L 3.379 0.878 L 11.627 12.677 L 9.835 12.677 L 1.587 0.878 Z"/></svg>
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The form element is the pink card itself rather than sitting inside one
        — same rendered result, one fewer wrapper. Shopify's injected hidden
        inputs are display: none, so they add no gap to the flex column.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- form 'contact', id: form_id, class: 'ness-contact__form' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Both states take focus on arrival: the form posts and reloads, so
          without this the outcome is announced to nobody.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Falls back to a real sentence rather than trusting the setting: an
          emptied field would otherwise seize focus with an empty live region
          that announces nothing, and paint a bare cream box.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          {%- assign success_text = section.settings.success_message
            | default: 'Thanks — we have your message and will be in touch.' -%}
          <p
            class="ness-contact__notice ness-contact__notice--success"
            role="status"
            tabindex="-1"
            autofocus
          >
            {{- success_text | escape -}}
          </p>
        {%- elsif form.errors -%}
          <div
            class="ness-contact__notice ness-contact__notice--error"
            id="{{ form_id }}-errors"
            role="alert"
            tabindex="-1"
            autofocus
          >
            <p class="ness-contact__notice-title">{{ 'templates.contact.form.error_heading' | t }}</p>
            <ul class="ness-contact__notice-list" role="list">
              {%- for field in form.errors -%}
                <li>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    'form' is Shopify's key for an error that belongs to no
                    single field, so there is nothing to link to.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- if field == 'form' -%}
                    {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    <a href="#{{ form_id }}-{{ field }}">
                      {{- form.errors.translated_fields[field] | capitalize }}
                      {{ form.errors.messages[field] -}}
                    </a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="ness-contact__field">
          <label class="ness-contact__label" for="{{ form_id }}-name">Name</label>
          <input
            id="{{ form_id }}-name"
            class="ness-contact__input"
            type="text"
            name="contact[name]"
            value="{% if form.name %}{{ form.name | escape }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.name | escape }}{% endif %}"
            placeholder="Ex. Park"
            autocomplete="name"
          >
        </div>

        <div class="ness-contact__field">
          <label class="ness-contact__label" for="{{ form_id }}-email">Email</label>
          <input
            id="{{ form_id }}-email"
            class="ness-contact__input"
            type="email"
            name="contact[email]"
            value="{% if form.email %}{{ form.email | escape }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.email | escape }}{% endif %}"
            placeholder="example@mail.com"
            autocomplete="email"
            spellcheck="false"
            autocapitalize="off"
            required
            aria-required="true"
            {% if form.errors contains 'email' %}
              aria-invalid="true"
              aria-describedby="{{ form_id }}-errors"
            {% endif %}
          >
        </div>

        <div class="ness-contact__field">
          <label class="ness-contact__label" for="{{ form_id }}-body">Write your message</label>
          <textarea
            id="{{ form_id }}-body"
            class="ness-contact__textarea"
            name="contact[body]"
            rows="5"
            placeholder="Write your brief"
            {% if form.errors contains 'body' %}
              aria-invalid="true"
              aria-describedby="{{ form_id }}-errors"
            {% endif %}
          >{{ form.body | escape }}</textarea>
        </div>

        <button type="submit" class="ness-contact__submit">Contact Us</button>
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Contact",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Wording is editable. The layout, the form's fields, and all colours and sizes are fixed by the design. Messages arrive at the email set in Settings → Notifications, and the sender's address is used as the reply-to."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Let’s Stay Connected" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body copy", "default": "Have questions or need assistance? We're here to help! Drop us a message and let’s connect. Whether you’re looking for expert advice, customization options, or just want to say hello, we’d love to hear from you. Let us help you find your perfect style!" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "success_message", "label": "Message after sending", "default": "Thanks for contacting us. We'll get back to you as soon as possible.", "info": "Appears above the fields, which stay on screen so another message can be sent. Error wording comes from Shopify and is not editable here." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Social links" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Set separately from the footer's social links, so the two can point at different places. Leave a field empty to hide that icon; leave all four empty to hide the row."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "social_heading", "label": "Row heading", "default": "Follow Us on Social Medias" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "social_facebook", "label": "Facebook" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "social_instagram", "label": "Instagram" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "social_youtube", "label": "YouTube" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "social_x", "label": "X" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
